 :pitfalls
 ["Do not start a fresh 5-second validator timeout."
  "Do not trust renderer self-validation or its requested validator revision."
  "Do not make worker_threads an assumed drop-in NBB runtime: it needs a qualified fixed boot path and termination semantics; child_process is already present and fits existing process-group cleanup."
  "Do not introduce a generic shell, -e execution surface or a selectable validator command. Fixed scripts only in production."
  "Do not clear operation timers merely because renderer close arrived."
  "Do not accumulate per-process cleanup budgets or leave validator ownership outside cleanup-holds."
  "Do not silently lower 64 targets, 64KiB/artifact, 1MiB stdout, or alter unsupported-bash behavior."
  "Do not claim moving validation alone fixes expensive synchronous work before spawn."
  "Do not confuse successful built-in JSON availability probe with a verified implementation."]
 :reflection {:lesson "A wire cap bounds memory, not the running time of an interpreted parser or portable digest. Keep deadline enforcement outside the expensive computation's execution thread and avoid reintroducing the same computation while importing its result."
